## memory: the first start of all 36 sidecars ran the devnet VM out of memory (2026-09-25T21:38Z)
  Each sidecar holds ~270 MB for its first ~2 minutes (the scrypt keystore, N=2^18, is opened once; the Go
  runtime returns the memory at its first forced GC, measured: 281 MB at 120 s, 16 MB at 150 s). 24 host
  sidecars starting within minutes exceeded the 7.7 GiB VM, the kernel OOM-killed processes (exit 137) and
  restarts kept it going. Fix: hosts h1/h2 recreated with GOMEMLIMIT=96MiB for their attached sidecars
  (docker/host.sh; their node is a separate process) and a 10 s stagger; supervised machines unchanged.
  No seat existed yet; the chain was unaffected (signers kept confirming every second).

